Snapshot chain test images

These files are generated by ../../generate_snapshot_test_images.py.

The chain contains:

* base.vmdk and base-s001.vmdk: uncompressed sparse base image
* snapshot1.vmdk and snapshot1-s001.vmdk: uncompressed sparse delta image
* snapshot2.vmdk: stream optimized compressed sparse image with embedded descriptor

The 64 KiB disk uses 8 KiB grains. The base image contains "B" in grains 0 and 2,
the first delta contains "M" in grain 1, and the active stream optimized image
contains "T" in grain 0. Grain 3 is sparse throughout the chain, so it reads as
zero bytes.

Descriptor modification times are set to 1000, 2000 and 3000 respectively. This
allows tests to select the base, first delta, or active image by timestamp.
